{"format":1,"seq":332,"writes":[{"type":"entry","value":{"model":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This looks like the same transient \"(failed)\" issue seen before — possibly the App token getting rejected on the first push attempt for a release branch lacking workflows. I'll just retry.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_bdrk_01WX8aucVQa8v1Xq19MttmPB","name":"typescript","arguments":{"code":"// @pit: {\"label\": \"Retry push of PR A branch and open the pull request\"}\nasync ({ git: { push }, gh: { prCreate } }, p: { body: string }) => {\n  const r = await push([\"-u\", \"origin\", \"ci/pi-assistant-install-deps\"]);\n  if (r.code) return r;\n  const pr = await prCreate({ base: \"main\", head: \"ci/pi-assistant-install-deps\", title: \"ci(pi-assistant): install locked dependencies before pi runs\", body: p.body });\n  return pr.stdout;\n}","params":{"body":"Refs #379 (area: CI workflow).\n\nThe pi-action job checks out a fresh tree with no `node_modules`. In the saved threads this caused:\n\n- 4 `tests.runTargeted` failures (368, 372 ×2, 375): `npx` silently fetched **vitest@5.1.0** from the registry, then failed with `Could not resolve 'vitest/config'`;\n- a `delivery.validate` dependency-check failure (366: `installed none`);\n- at least 4 manual `execFile(\"npm\", [\"ci\"])` calls to recover.\n\nThis adds the same Node setup and `npm ci` steps `ci.yml` uses (pinned `setup-node`, lockfile-compatible npm 12.2.0) after checkout, so the delivery helpers work on their first call."}}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"nvidia","model":"aws/anthropic/bedrock-claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":592,"cacheRead":72206,"cacheWrite":951,"totalTokens":73751,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":false},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":56},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794645792830,"responseId":"msg_bdrk_vswnae6onus6wriskxlsqhhqbwfk6xtdkmayxm6czne2y3y3dqsq",